{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/807581-steven-universe-crystal-gems-are-alien-demons","id":807581,"title":"Steven Universe - Crystal Gems are Alien Demons(?)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-12T21:08:11-08:00","id":807581,"title":"Steven Universe - Crystal Gems are Alien Demons(?)","content":"Not looking for any campaign guidelines but after Watching &quot;The Answer&quot; episode an idea stuck me, The Homeworld is made up of hilariously short-sighted angels and the Crystal Gems fell because they where tired of being treated like possessions! Think about it, Homeworld Tech is so incredibly dangerous that just allowing it to exist could irreparably damage the very fabric of the world and nearly every Gem that decided to help Steven did so after a long period of discovering that home-world gems are completely in the wrong when it comes to information on earth. What do you think of this idea with the confines of the world of darkness?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/885-bwgustaf","name":"bwgustaf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T10:07:46-08:00","id":807981,"title":"","content":"*general spoiler warning for the entirety of the series up to and including &quot;Log Date 7 15 2&quot;*<br /> <br /> Having Homeworld as an analog for the God-Machine works really, really well in light of recent episodes. The whole &quot;terraform for maximum efficiency&quot; is exactly the kind of thing the G-M might call for. Based on that, maybe Homeworld is where the G-M resides, and it has completely taken over; there's no longer humanity there (or alien equivalents), just Gems/Angels. So now the Homeworld-Machine is looking to expand, to take over and normalize other worlds so they run at peak efficiency. It's refined the process of creating angels into Kindergardens, where it can create hundreds at once.<br /> <br /> And since the Homeworld-Machine is very far away, and doesn't have great surveillance on Earth, it lets the Crystal Gems be in their demon forms exclusively, without worrying as much about Cover. I remember seeing something about demons fusing together to grant themselves greater powers, but I forget if that was in a book or it was a hack I saw here; either way, that super works.<br /> <br /> Quartzes, Amethysts, and the like are Destroyers (&quot;huge, loyal soldiers&quot;), while Gems like Jaspers and Rubies are Guardians. Peridots are Analysts (and maybe Diamonds are too, or at least Yellow Diamond). Sapphires and Lapis Lazulis fit best as Psychopomps, I think. I suppose that means Pearls are Messengers, with the caveat of Homeworld-Machine not needing them as much, because it doesn't have any masses it needs to communicate with, so they've been demoted to status symbols. Maybe Sapphires are also Messengers, I'm not sure.<br /> <br /> It's pretty clear our Ruby and Sapphire fell for love, and remain fused. They're probably both Saboteurs. Pearl fell when Rose Quartz did, and seems like she'd fit as an Inquisitor. Amethyst fits a lot of the behavior of a Tempter, though the others keep her focused. Peridot's an Integrator, no question. Rose herself might have been a Saboteur, not sure.<br /> <br /> Steven's clearly a demon-child, probably a Fractal. The shattered gems they fight seem like the gem version of Pandorans, rather than Cryptids or Stygmatics. But Greg is probably Stygmatic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T10:51:12-08:00","id":808036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/807581-steven-universe-crystal-gems-are-alien-demons?p=807981#post807981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*general spoiler warning for the entirety of the series up to and including &quot;Log Date 7 15 2&quot;*<br /> <br /> Having Homeworld as an analog for the God-Machine works really, really well in light of recent episodes. The whole &quot;terraform for maximum efficiency&quot; is exactly the kind of thing the G-M might call for. Based on that, maybe Homeworld is where the G-M resides, and it has completely taken over; there's no longer humanity there (or alien equivalents), just Gems/Angels. So now the Homeworld-Machine is looking to expand, to take over and normalize other worlds so they run at peak efficiency. It's refined the process of creating angels into Kindergardens, where it can create hundreds at once.<br /> <br /> And since the Homeworld-Machine is very far away, and doesn't have great surveillance on Earth, it lets the Crystal Gems be in their demon forms exclusively, without worrying as much about Cover. I remember seeing something about demons fusing together to grant themselves greater powers, but I forget if that was in a book or it was a hack I saw here; either way, that super works.<br /> <br /> Quartzes, Amethysts, and the like are Destroyers (&quot;huge, loyal soldiers&quot;), while Gems like Jaspers and Rubies are Guardians. Peridots are Analysts (and maybe Diamonds are too, or at least Yellow Diamond). Sapphires and Lapis Lazulis fit best as Psychopomps, I think. I suppose that means Pearls are Messengers, with the caveat of Homeworld-Machine not needing them as much, because it doesn't have any masses it needs to communicate with, so they've been demoted to status symbols. Maybe Sapphires are also Messengers, I'm not sure.<br /> <br /> It's pretty clear our Ruby and Sapphire fell for love, and remain fused. They're probably both Saboteurs. Pearl fell when Rose Quartz did, and seems like she'd fit as an Inquisitor. Amethyst fits a lot of the behavior of a Tempter, though the others keep her focused. Peridot's an Integrator, no question. Rose herself might have been a Saboteur, not sure.<br /> <br /> Steven's clearly a demon-child, probably a Fractal. The shattered gems they fight seem like the gem version of Pandorans, rather than Cryptids or Stygmatics. But Greg is probably Stygmatic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with most of the stuff except for Yellow Diamond in &quot;Message Received&quot; because shifting between being extremely angry and not showing emotion at all seems like Exileish Behavior. Maybe Exile with some Analyst Embeds throw in for &quot;Flavor&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/885-bwgustaf","name":"bwgustaf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T11:25:57-08:00","id":808075,"title":"","content":"Merge is a Exploit in the core book. It actually makes sense for &quot;bad&quot; gems too! They use the exploit to increase their power and the process screws them over because using the exploit's required empathy is literarly against their programming!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/885-bwgustaf","name":"bwgustaf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T16:04:14-08:00","id":808301,"title":"","content":"In this context, one could construe &quot;The Return/Jailbreak&quot; as the story of Jasper's Fall. She begins to become somewhat erratic when she confronts Steven, who she thinks is Rose under a new Cover. She is still fixated on Rose from all those millennia ago, and in this schema, may have been made to hunt her down. She outright deviates from her mission, choosing to focus on &quot;Rose&quot;, and in the end choses to Fuse with Lapis, despite the fact that this appears to be the sort of thing Homeworld would kill her for. Just goes to show that a Fall is not necessarily a reformation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T10:53:36-08:00","id":808841,"title":"","content":"So does demon the descent have any rules on synchronization? The short on fusion says that gems need to be perfectly synchronized physically, emotionally, and mentally in order to fuse. It seems that malachite is fused mentallly but not physically or emotionally, while the crystal gems seem to be getting the handle on the emotional aspect pretty well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/885-bwgustaf","name":"bwgustaf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}